{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Matches — UCESCO Volunteer Manager{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="mb-2 flex items-center justify-between">
        <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">Matches</h1>
        <twig:ExportMenu route="match_export" />
    </div>

    {#
        The rule in words, for the Volunteer Manager. It is ProgramMatchFinder's
        rule (ADR 0042): change one, change both.
    #}
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
        Volunteers who can be at a program and have a reason to fit it, best fits first. The choice is yours.
    </p>
    <details class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600" data-match-explainer>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-brand-600 hover:underline">How matches are found</summary>
        <div class="mt-2 max-w-3xl space-y-2 rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">
            <p>A volunteer is suggested for a program when both are true:</p>
            <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5">
                <li><strong>They can be there:</strong> they have a stay at the program's branch that hasn't ended and overlaps the program's dates.</li>
                <li>
                    <strong>They have a reason to fit:</strong>
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
                        <li><strong>Skills</strong> — they hold at least one of the program's recommended skills, or</li>
                        <li><strong>Experience</strong> — they have already done one of the program's activity types, in any program. These rows are marked <em>By experience</em>, and <em>Not on profile</em> shows the skills you could tick on their profile.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p><strong>Order:</strong> most matching skills first, then the most past activities of the program's types, then volunteers present now before upcoming ones. Programs that have gone longest without an activity come first; programs that haven't started yet come last.</p>
            <p>The app only knows that an activity was logged, not whether it went well — treat the order as a suggestion.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600" data-more-matches-explainer>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-brand-600 hover:underline">How to get more matches</summary>
        <div class="mt-2 max-w-3xl space-y-2 rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">
            <p>Most matches come from skills, so ticking skills is what brings more of them. The lists below the matches show where to start:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
                <li><strong>Available volunteers with no skills</strong> — here now or arriving later, with nothing ticked on their profile. Tick what they can do, and they can be suggested on skills, not only on past activities.</li>
                <li><strong>Programs with no recommended skills</strong> — tick the skills they need. Until then, only volunteers who have already done their activities can be suggested.</li>
                <li><strong>Programs with only one recommended skill</strong> — add the others they need. A single skill matches few people.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Matches on experience grow by themselves as activities are logged.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <form
        method="get"
        data-turbo-action="replace"
        class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-600 print:hidden"
        data-controller="auto-submit"
        data-match-filters
    >
        <label for="match-branch" class="sr-only">Branch</label>
        <select id="match-branch" name="branch" class="max-w-full rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-1 text-sm focus:border-brand-500 focus:outline-none" data-action="change->auto-submit#submit">
            <option value="">All branches</option>
            {% for option in branchOptions %}
                <option value="{{ option.id }}" {{ filters.branch and filters.branch.id == option.id ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ option.name }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
        <label for="match-program" class="sr-only">Program</label>
        <select id="match-program" name="program" class="max-w-full rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-1 text-sm focus:border-brand-500 focus:outline-none" data-action="change->auto-submit#submit">
            <option value="">All programs</option>
            {% for option in programOptions %}
                <option value="{{ option.id }}" {{ filters.program and filters.program.id == option.id ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ option.project.branch.name }} › {{ option.name }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
        <label for="match-who" class="sr-only">Who</label>
        <select id="match-who" name="who" class="max-w-full rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-1 text-sm focus:border-brand-500 focus:outline-none" data-action="change->auto-submit#submit">
            <option value="">Present and upcoming</option>
            {% for option in whoOptions %}
                <option value="{{ option.value }}" {{ filters.who is same as(option) ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ option.label }} only</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
        <button type="submit" class="sr-only">Filter</button>

        {% if filters.branch or filters.program or filters.who is not null %}
            <a href="{{ path('match_index') }}" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" data-turbo-action="replace">Clear filters</a>
        {% endif %}
    </form>

    {% if groups is empty and noSkills is empty %}
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">No open program matches these filters.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="space-y-4">
        {% for group in groups %}
            {% set matches = group.matches %}
            {% set program = matches.program %}
            <section class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm" aria-labelledby="program-{{ program.id }}-heading" data-program-matches="{{ program.id }}">
                <div class="border-b border-slate-200 px-5 py-4">
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">{{ program.project.branch.name }} › {{ program.project.name }}</p>
                    <h2 id="program-{{ program.id }}-heading" class="font-semibold">{{ program.name }}</h2>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
                        {% if program.skills is empty %}
                            No recommended skills yet — <a href="{{ path('program_edit', {id: program.id}) }}" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">tick them</a>.
                        {% else %}
                            Needs: {{ program.skills|map(s => s.name)|sort|join(', ') }}
                        {% endif %}
                    </p>
                    <p class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-xs text-slate-500" data-need>
                        <span>
                            {%- if matches.notStarted -%}
                                Starts {{ program.startDate|date('j M Y') }}
                            {%- elseif matches.daysSinceLastActivity is null -%}
                                No activity yet
                            {%- elseif matches.daysSinceLastActivity < 0 -%}
                                Activity planned {{ matches.lastActivity|date('j M Y') }}
                            {%- elseif matches.daysSinceLastActivity == 0 -%}
                                Last activity today
                            {%- else -%}
                                Last activity {{ matches.daysSinceLastActivity }} day{{ matches.daysSinceLastActivity == 1 ? '' : 's' }} ago
                            {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                        {% if program.endDate %}<span>Ends {{ program.endDate|date('j M Y') }}</span>{% endif %}
                        {% if matches.candidates is not empty %}<span>{{ matches.candidates|length }} candidate{{ matches.candidates|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>{% endif %}
                    </p>
                    {% if matches.uncoveredSkills is not empty %}
                        <p class="mt-2 inline-block rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-amber-800" data-uncovered>
                            Nobody available for: {{ matches.uncoveredSkills|map(s => s.name)|join(', ') }}
                        </p>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>

                {% if matches.candidates is empty %}
                    <p class="px-5 py-6 text-sm text-slate-500">No available volunteer has these skills or this experience.</p>
                {% else %}
                    <div class="p-3">
                        <twig:DataTable :columns="columns" :rows="group.rows" />
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </section>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# What to tick for more matches; "How to get more matches" above explains it. #}
    {# Always shown, even empty: an empty list is the good news. #}
    <section class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-600" aria-labelledby="volunteers-no-skills-heading" data-volunteers-no-skills>
        <h2 id="volunteers-no-skills-heading" class="font-semibold text-slate-800">Available volunteers with no skills ({{ volunteersWithoutSkills|length }})</h2>
        {% if volunteersWithoutSkills is empty %}
            <p class="mt-2 text-slate-500">Every volunteer with a current or upcoming stay has at least one skill on their profile.</p>
        {% else %}
            <ul class="mt-2 columns-1 gap-6 sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3">
                {% for stay in volunteersWithoutSkills %}
                    <li><a href="{{ path('volunteer_edit', {id: stay.volunteer.id}) }}" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">{{ stay.volunteer.fullName }}</a> <span class="text-slate-400">· {{ stay.branch.name }} · {{ stay.covers(today) ? 'here until ' ~ stay.endDate|date('j M Y') : 'arrives ' ~ stay.startDate|date('j M Y') }}</span></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    {% if noSkills is not empty %}
        <section class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-600" aria-labelledby="no-skills-heading" data-no-skills>
            <h2 id="no-skills-heading" class="font-semibold text-slate-800">Programs with no recommended skills ({{ noSkills|length }})</h2>
            <ul class="mt-2 columns-1 gap-6 sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3">
                {% for matches in noSkills %}
                    {% set program = matches.program %}
                    <li><a href="{{ path('program_edit', {id: program.id}) }}" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">{{ program.name }}</a> <span class="text-slate-400">· {{ program.project.branch.name }}{{ matches.candidates is not empty ? ' · also shown above' }}</span></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if oneSkill is not empty %}
        <section class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-600" aria-labelledby="one-skill-heading" data-one-skill>
            <h2 id="one-skill-heading" class="font-semibold text-slate-800">Programs with only one recommended skill ({{ oneSkill|length }})</h2>
            <ul class="mt-2 columns-1 gap-6 sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3">
                {% for program in oneSkill %}
                    <li><a href="{{ path('program_edit', {id: program.id}) }}" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">{{ program.name }}</a> <span class="text-slate-400">· {{ program.project.branch.name }} · {{ program.skills.first.name }}</span></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
